3. Training data for the shipped weights  --  COMMISSIONED, NO ONWARD RESTRICTION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

No dataset is redistributed here; data/raw, data/preprocessed, data/manual and
runs/ are all gitignored. docs/EarLandmarker_web.onnx IS tracked, and as of this
version it is trained on ONE source:

| source      | samples | images                        | annotations        |
|-------------|---------|-------------------------------|--------------------|
| manual      |  10,535 | collected from the wild,      | commissioned       |
|             |         | vetted to exclude non-        | work-for-hire via  |
|             |         | permissive/non-commercial     | a crowd-annotation |
|             |         | licences                      | platform           |

The annotations follow the 55-point ear convention (iBUG's point ordering:
0-19 outer helix, 20-34 inner helix, 35-49 concha border, 50-54 superior crus).
The CONVENTION is a numbering scheme, not a dataset; no iBUG annotation data is
used, redistributed or derived from in these weights.

The weights are offered under Apache-2.0, the same as the code.

DISCLOSURE -- MODEL-ASSISTED ANNOTATION
The annotation task was seeded with predictions from an earlier model
(v6_persp65) which annotators then corrected, rather than being drawn from
scratch. That earlier model was trained on the iBUG-derived corpus described in
section 4, and iBUG's terms reach "any portion of derived data". The copyright
holder's position is that human correction of a machine-proposed starting point
produces an independent work: measured on this set, the final labels differ from
the seeding model's prediction by more than one pixel (at 192px) on 51% of all
points, with a median displacement of ~1px against ~4px for annotation of the
same model's own training distribution.

This is recorded because it is a judgment call rather than a clean chain, and
anyone relying on these weights should be able to see the basis for it. If you
need provenance with no such question attached, retrain on annotations drawn
from scratch; scripts/ingest_manual.py takes any directory of image +
55-line "x y" annotation pairs.

